Date: Wed, 8 Sep 93 23:32:07 PDT
From: szabo@netcom.com (Nick Szabo)
Subject: Offense vs. defense: fundamental politcal insight

Paul BaClace: 
> The relative cost-effectiveness of defensive and offensive technology is
> important...
> 	dD/dO   { delta Defensive weapon cost / delta Offensive weapon cost }

This key insight should be used as a central tenent of political action,
hopefully in most cases substituting peaceful "munitions" like
cryptography, contracts, and free markets for weapons.  This
insight has some very critical near-term applications; it need
not be confined to the fun but speculative discussions of "nanarchy".
For example, encryption and traffic-analysis-defeating remailers 
make violation of information privacy orders of magnitude more 
difficult than current methods (wiretapping, searching physical mail,
grepping cleartext e-mail spool files, etc.).  Much political
power is based, in one way or another, on the ability to snoop.

